Qwen3.8-Flash-Next MTP patch 02: the draft head on three cards.

vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/mtp.py

Needs flash-next-mtp-01-enable.patch and flash-next-mem-01-pp-embed-head.patch.

On 3 x RTX 3090 the drafter sits on the last pipeline rank next to 15 body
layers (VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION=16,17,15) and its INT4 routed experts. Two of
its own tensors do not need to be on that GPU:

- lm_head. The drafter built a quantized copy of the target's head, only for
  load_eagle_model() to replace it with the target's own head, which is on
  the same rank, right after loading. Building it cost its Marlin repack
  (0.6 GiB) during the load. It is now a PPMissingLayer, and the loader skips
  the checkpoint's lm_head for it.
- embed_tokens. Under PP > 1 the drafter keeps its own input embedding
  (0.60 GiB INT8), from which a step gathers a few rows. With
  VLLM_MTP_EMBED_ON_HOST=1 (the default) it is built and loaded on the host,
  and after loading its table is left in pinned host memory behind a UVA view.

